      "id": 10,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "## Reading these panels\n\n| Question | Where to look |\n| --- | --- |\n| What did this container print? | **Live logs**, filtered by the `service` selector above. Unstructured lines are here and only here. |\n| Is anything failing right now? | **Errors and warnings by service** — a spike, then the **Errors** counter. |\n| Who was refused, and for what? | **Blocked and refused**, then the log lines panel beside it. |\n| Which flow was this line part of? | The **TraceID** link on any line that carries a `traceparent`, which opens the trace in Jaeger. |\n| Was anything actually *decided*? | The audit dashboard at **http://localhost:8088/dashboard** — the log store is not the audit trail, and a verdict belongs in the record that outlives these logs. |\n\nLogs here are kept for **7 days** (`retention_period` in `observability/loki/loki-config.yml`, enforced by the compactor); the audit trail has its own retention (`TELEMETRY_RETENTION`, 30 days by default) because a debug log and a security record have different lifetimes.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.1.0",
      "title": "How to read this",
      "type": "text"
